<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pyotr Masherov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1918">1918</a>–<a href="/years/1980">1980</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pyotr Masherov was a Soviet Belarusian leader, a partisan commander in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> and Hero of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>. As first secretary of the Communist Party of Byelorussia from 1965 to 1980 he oversaw rapid industrial growth and the commemoration of the war. He died in a car crash in 1980.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pyotr-masherov.jpg" alt="Pyotr Masherov" width="320" height="437" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: post of Belarus; derivative work by Makakaaaa · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pyotr_Masherov.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
